{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of the source-facing polynomial-cube exclusion at actual partial degrees (6,9).  From literal bivariate polynomials of outer degrees six and nine, leading coefficients s^6 and s^9 for a common polynomial s, and nonzero constant Keller bracket, the formalization proves that no such source exists, including when s is constant.  It constructs the finite-pole or infinity expansion, exhausts every timing of the eight Faber loads through rho2, and excludes the remaining elliptic, cusp, zero-invariant, and constant-core terminal fibres.  It does not claim the reduction from an arbitrary Keller pair, all (6,9), maximum eleven, or the plane Jacobian conjecture.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Dan Clemens Posch"
    }
  ],
